---
title: Local load testing
intent: Run a short, rate-limited load probe against the local fixture.
group: automation
features:
- perf
command: curlew perf perf-local.yaml --vus 1 --duration 1s --rps 5 --output perf-results.json
order: 130
runnable: true
---

Distributed workers are not part of the CLI. This example uses one process, one virtual user, a one-second duration and a small request rate. The perf command accepts a single request file and can write JSON or HTML reports; it does not accept run’s variable flags. Run load tests only against a server you are authorized to exercise.

## Prerequisites

Use the complete repository checkout and start Mudflat as described in the [cookbook setup](https://github.com/weiqigod/curlew/blob/main/site/README.md). Run these commands from the repository root with `curlew` on PATH.

```bash
export MUDFLAT_URL="${MUDFLAT_URL:-http://127.0.0.1:18080}"
export MUDFLAT_WS_URL="${MUDFLAT_WS_URL:-ws://127.0.0.1:18080}"
export RUN_ID="cookbook-$(date +%s)-$$"
```

## Run it

```bash
printf 'name: Local performance probe\nrequest:\n  method: GET\n  url: "%s/echo"\n' "$MUDFLAT_URL" > perf-local.yaml
curlew perf perf-local.yaml --vus 1 --duration 1s --rps 5 --output perf-results.json
```

A successful execution exits 0. Read assertion outcomes as well as the exit code.
No example output or timing numbers are fabricated here.

## Complete collection

<!-- cookbook-source: examples/cookbook/perf.yaml -->
```yaml
name: Local performance probe
request:
  method: GET
  url: "http://127.0.0.1:18080/echo"
```
